<title>BRAZIL: Brazil bolsa says CVRD sale valid.</title>
<headline>Brazil bolsa says CVRD sale valid.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Rio de Janeiro bolsa considers the auction of Brazilian mining group CVRD valid despite a last-minute court injunction apparently suspending the effects of the sale, a spokeswoman said.</p>
<p>The spokeswoman said the sale of CVRD for 3.338 billion reais to the Valepar consortium was completed at 1750 local/2050 GMT, but the injunction only arrived at 1840 local time.</p>
<p>She added that government lawyers would nevertheless study the injunction.</p>
<p>Court officials say the injunction was issued at 1745 local.</p>
<p>The Valepar consortium led by Brazilian steelmaker CSN bought 41.73 percent of CVRD's voting shares in the auction of a controlling stake.</p>
<p>((-- Fatima Cristina, Rio newsroom 55-21-5074151))</p>
